cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenMC reproduction of an LBE fuel-assembly benchmark (Energies 18 (2025) 3564) and analysis of the k_eff discrepancy"
abstract: >-
  OpenMC 0.16 model of a lead-bismuth eutectic cooled fast reactor fuel assembly
  (91 pins, 5 rings, P/D = 1.7144, annular UO2 pellet, HT-9 structure) with a
  self-built continuous-energy ENDF/B-VIII.0 library (IAEA NDS + NJOY2016).
  The model reproduces the calculation workflow of the reference paper and shows,
  through a packing upper bound and an enrichment study, that the published
  k_eff reference (1.31181 at 14.83 % 235U) is inconsistent with the material and
  geometry data of the same paper (it corresponds to about 24 % enrichment).
  The cross-section chain is independently validated with the Godiva benchmark
  (k = 1.00071 +/- 0.00073).
type: software
license: MIT
keywords:
  - OpenMC
  - Monte Carlo
  - lead-cooled fast reactor
  - LBE
  - criticality benchmark
  - ENDF/B-VIII.0
  - NJOY
